title: MikroTik REST API: IP Pools
agents: mikrotik_rest_api
catalog: hw/network/mikrotik
license: GPL
distribution: check_mk
description:
 Usage of the IP pools of a MikroTik router ({/ip/pool}) as used by the
 DHCP server, PPP or hotspot. The agent counts the used addresses from
 {/ip/pool/used}; the leases themselves are not transferred.

 The pool size is computed from the ranges (from-to, prefix or single
 address, several separated by commas). Levels via the rule {MikroTik
 REST API: IP pools}: used addresses in percent (default 80%/90%) and
 optionally free addresses. A configured next pool is shown.

 Special agent {MikroTik RouterOS (mikrotik-rest-api)} in Setup >
 Agents > Other integrations, module "IP pools".

 Added in mikrotik-rest-api 1.1.0 by Klaus Paulitsch.

item:
 The name of the pool.

perfdata:
 Used addresses in percent, used and free addresses.

inventory:
 One service per pool.
